  "comment": [
    "Verified-model matrix row -> exact GGUF filename table (T136.6).",
    "",
    "This table is the ONLY way the parity suite is allowed to turn a matrix row into",
    "a GGUF file. Directory scanning ('first *.gguf in the directory', the findGGUF",
    "pattern at inference/inference.go:317) is banned for parity/bench because the",
    "flagship models are staged FLAT in /var/lib/zerfoo/models: every row pointed at",
    "that directory resolved to the alphabetically-first file and the whole matrix",
    "went green while proving nothing. See docs/lore.md L-0018.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  row            stable matrix-row key; referenced by ModelParityConfig.MatrixRow",
    "  label          human label, matches docs/verified-models.md",
    "  model_dir_env  env var naming the DIRECTORY the pinned file lives in",
    "  file           exact filename, joined onto the directory; \"\" = not staged",
    "  architecture   expected GGUF general.architecture (asserted per row)",
    "  gguf_name      expected GGUF general.name when the file declares one",
    "  size_bytes     expected file size when pinned; 0 = unchecked",
    "",
    "architecture is corroboration, NOT identity: 'llama' covers both Llama 3.2 and",
    "Mistral, and 'qwen2' covers both Qwen2-7B and the DeepSeek-R1 distill, so an",
    "architecture-only check would still have passed the vacuous matrix. The exact",
    "path is the identity assertion."
